{
  "schema": "enforcement-posture-conformance/1",
  "package_version": "0.5.0",
  "note": "Language-agnostic conformance vectors. An implementation in any language conforms if it reproduces every `expect` from the corresponding `input`. The refusal cases \u2014 incomparable, split, uncovered \u2014 are the point: they are what a reimplementation gets wrong, and getting them wrong turns a refusal into a false assurance.",
